cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "AMP-ML: A Reproducible Machine Learning Benchmark for Antimicrobial Peptide Classification"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible machine learning benchmark for antimicrobial peptide (AMP)
  binary classification. The pipeline extracts 4,921 physicochemical and
  sequence-derived descriptors from peptide sequences, selects 300 features via
  a five-method competition, trains six models under nested cross-validation,
  and evaluates them on a held-out independent test set (n=384) that is never
  used for model selection. The repository ships a one-command reproduction
  pipeline (run_all.sh), an environment self-check, a five-layer independent
  verification audit covering 30 numerical checks, SHAP-based feature
  attribution, publication-ready figures, and an explicit audit of negative-sample
  distribution bias.
